#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096842 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096401 :question/id #uuid "8fcdb2c8-71ca-5bfa-b7fe-49f8f2c05bbb" :question/math-academy-id "e-182" :question/problem "Given that $y = \\sqrt{1-x^2},$ find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x}.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x}.\n$$\n\nHere, we've used $u$ instead of $g$ for the intermediate variable. \n\nLet $u=1-x^2.$ Then $y = \\sqrt u = u^{1/2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u} = \\dfrac{1}{2}u^{-1/2} = \\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt u}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x}  = -2x.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (-2x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{2\\sqrt{u}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f0cdac9-57b2-5634-8d98-d6adf8a85204" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186657684 :question-generator/id #uuid "eb1e532d-86c7-511f-9e95-e418689ac150" :question-generator/script "generators/f2/f2e28f3a0d0677c48b52dfa4d9467314a67845f5b1a52d46a7e19b565e72c024/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097251 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "256d8104-e561-50d4-bb47-c84cda5f979d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{(5x-1{)}^{3}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327259} {:answer/id #uuid "92909c43-4d9f-55c2-9367-b2903d4d10f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328210} {:answer/id #uuid "b84fdb58-69a3-5339-b857-edeff32c5507" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5x-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328539} {:answer/id #uuid "ccdb8149-860b-5213-8db1-d9